#
# Counter-example for the native math:MissingProbabilityModelLowering gate: a world
# references a probability model through logic:probabilityModel, but that model
# individual is typed as a plain math:MathematicalObject (a non-dependency-model class)
# and declares NO math:probabilityModelLowering — neither directly nor class-level. The
# native gate MUST emit math:MissingProbabilityModelLowering (and no other probability
# failure class): absent a lowering the engine reports unsupported, never assumes
# independence.
# Back-reference: math:probabilityModelLowering / math:MissingProbabilityModelLowering (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:world logic:probabilityModel ex:unloweredModel .

ex:unloweredModel a math:MathematicalObject .
